commit 5bdb7f6cf0ee1a4f471a0c612f1eb2d00ac82c67

C03: the recipient question asks whom BAXY should answer, never hands the reply to the person (MESSAGING1365)

MESSAGING1363 measured H0045 and H0074: the recipient clarification for «contestale que llego en 10» and «contestale que sí» was rendered as «A quién le vas a contestar que…» (the person executing the reply, once also «llegó» for «llego»), while «¿A quién le quieres responder?» passed.

llm.formulate_explicit_clarification_question: for message.send missing the recipient, a question that assigns the answering to the person (vas a / le contestas / le respondes / you will reply…) or that does not ask whom is corrected once with the contract (BAXY answers on the person's behalf; keep what they want to say as said) and fails on repeat, like the which-alarm and the past-action checks.

No .NET change. Offline syntax check only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


